---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="What Happens If You Skip Licensing — LicensingMadeSimple" description="The real consequences of operating without proper licenses.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>What Happens If You Skip It</h1>
      <p>The real consequences of operating without proper licenses.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container article" style="max-width: 720px;">
      <h2>Fines</h2>
      <p>Most jurisdictions impose fines for operating without required licenses. These range from a few hundred dollars for a missing city business license to tens of thousands for operating without a required state financial services license. Fines are often per-violation, meaning each day of unlicensed operation can be a separate fine.</p>

      <h2>Forced Shutdown</h2>
      <p>Government agencies can issue cease-and-desist orders requiring you to stop operating immediately until you're properly licensed. For financial services, this can happen fast — state regulators actively monitor for unlicensed operators.</p>

      <h2>Contract Problems</h2>
      <p>Contracts you sign while unlicensed may be unenforceable. If you're a contractor without a license and a client doesn't pay, you may not be able to pursue them in court. The client can use your unlicensed status as a defense.</p>

      <h2>Personal Liability</h2>
      <p>Operating without a license can pierce the corporate veil — the legal protection that normally keeps business liabilities separate from your personal assets. If something goes wrong while you're unlicensed, you could be personally liable.</p>

      <h2>The Fix Is Usually Simpler Than You Think</h2>
      <p>Most licensing issues are fixable. The process is straightforward once you know what you need, and professional help makes it faster. The biggest cost isn't the service fee — it's the revenue you lose while you're unable to operate.</p>

      <p><a href="/#wizard">Get your licensing roadmap</a> in 30 seconds and find out exactly what you need.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .article h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 32px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .article h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .article p { font-size: 0.93rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 14px; }
</style>
